INT. BELL TOWER OF THE DROWNED CHAPEL - DUSK

A chapel sunk to its rafters in a black lake. The bell tower pokes above the water like a stubborn finger. Lantern light. Fish scales glitter on the beams.

ORSOLYA VANE (40s, ferrywoman, salt-cracked hands) ladles broth into tin cups. Beside her, TEMBO ADEYEMI-LUND (20s, apprentice cartographer, ink on every cuff) unrolls a map.

A HOODED STRANGER sits apart, back to the wall, a staff across his knees.

ORSOLYA
Eat. The lake gives nothing back after dark.

TEMBO
The map says the shoals are east of us.

ORSOLYA
The map says a lot of things.

Behind them, PIP (12, barefoot, a ferry rat) dangles from a rafter, grinning.

PIP
I counted the bells. There's four.

TEMBO
There were three on the chart --

ORSOLYA
Pip, get down --

STRANGER
(quietly)
He's right. Four.

PIP
Told you!

ORSOLYA
Who asked you?

TEMBO
(over her)
Four? Where's the fourth?

STRANGER
Where it always was.

Silence. The water laps. The broth steams. Everything is calm.

The Stranger lowers his hood. Pale eyes, a bell-metal collar fused to his throat.

STRANGER (CONT'D)
My name is Corvane. I was the fourth.

Below them, the water goes perfectly still. Then every lantern gutters at once.

ORSOLYA
Pip. Tembo. Behind me.

CORVANE
Too late for that, ferrywoman.

PIP
He's ringing!

A deep toll rolls up from under the lake. The floorboards shake.

TEMBO
Make it stop!

ORSOLYA
(to herself)
Should have left him on the shore.

CORVANE
Tonight, you ring with me.
